WEBVTT

00:02.880 --> 00:05.090
A long, long time ago.

00:05.300 --> 00:08.170
A story from about a hundred years ago.

00:08.970 --> 00:13.430
Nadja, guided by destiny, arrived in Italy

00:17.470 --> 00:18.770
NAAJA

00:17.470 --> 00:18.770
Nadja,

00:18.890 --> 00:21.440
With your eyes

00:18.890 --> 00:21.440
Kimi no hitomi ni wa

00:21.440 --> 00:22.650
Nadja,

00:21.440 --> 00:22.650
NAAJA

00:22.690 --> 00:24.940
What do you see?

00:22.690 --> 00:24.940
Nani ga mieru

00:24.980 --> 00:27.860
Shining in the far distance,

00:24.980 --> 00:27.860
Haruka tooku hikaru

00:27.860 --> 00:30.240
The door to the future,

00:27.860 --> 00:30.240
Mirai no tobira

00:31.160 --> 00:34.620
That's what I'm searching for

00:31.160 --> 00:34.620
Sagashite iru

00:34.620 --> 00:41.830
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:42.540 --> 00:46.040
If everyone could meet with a smile

00:42.540 --> 00:46.040
Minna egao de aetara

00:46.130 --> 00:49.380
I'm sure there would be no more fighting

00:46.130 --> 00:49.380
Arasoi mo kitto nakunaru

00:49.420 --> 00:52.630
It could be so much more fun

00:49.420 --> 00:52.630
Konna ni mo tanoshi kunaru

00:52.680 --> 00:56.100
The world is wide, but it's still one

00:52.680 --> 00:56.100
Sekai wa hiroi kedo hitotsu ne

00:56.470 --> 00:59.770
I can't see the end of the journey

00:56.470 --> 00:59.770
Tabi no owari wa mienai

00:59.890 --> 01:03.230
God is the only one who could possibly know

00:59.890 --> 01:03.230
Kamisama ga tabun shitteru

01:03.400 --> 01:06.980
To the people who, someday, I will meet again

01:03.400 --> 01:06.980
Itsukamata deaeru hito tachi ni

01:07.020 --> 01:09.150
I will go waving

01:07.020 --> 01:09.150
Te wo furinagara

01:09.230 --> 01:15.910
Sometimes, there are days I feel blue,

01:09.230 --> 01:15.910
Toki ni wa BURUU ni naru hi mo aru kedo

01:15.950 --> 01:18.660
But I won't look back

01:15.950 --> 01:18.660
Ushiro mukanai

01:18.990 --> 01:23.960
Until the day my dream comes true

01:18.990 --> 01:23.960
Yume ga kanau hi made

01:24.250 --> 01:27.670
Nadja, Your smile

01:24.250 --> 01:27.670
NAAJA kimi no hohoemi wa

01:27.750 --> 01:31.090
Nadja, gives me courage

01:27.750 --> 01:31.090
NAAJA yuuki ni naru

01:31.130 --> 01:34.050
Under the blue sky,

01:31.130 --> 01:34.050
Aoi sora no shita de

01:34.180 --> 01:37.010
I will find the place

01:34.180 --> 01:37.010
Ashita no yukue

01:37.300 --> 01:41.230
where my future lies

01:37.300 --> 01:41.230
Mitsukeru kara

01:55.970 --> 02:01.100
﻿I was able to meet Count Capuletti of Milan who was mentioned in my mother's diary.

02:01.680 --> 02:04.180
﻿However, he didn't remember my mother.

02:05.100 --> 02:07.190
﻿He used to be a rich man.

02:07.360 --> 02:09.230
But, now... because of Antonio...

02:18.660 --> 02:19.910
﻿Terrible!

02:20.620 --> 02:21.740
﻿It's just too terrible!

02:22.200 --> 02:24.410
D﻿-Did I do something?

02:25.290 --> 02:26.790
﻿N-No, no!

02:27.120 --> 02:29.210
I ﻿was just thinking about Antonio...

02:29.960 --> 02:33.170
﻿To drive someone into bankruptcy in order to make money...!

02:33.380 --> 02:35.340
﻿He's inhuman!

02:36.760 --> 02:38.180
﻿Nadja, that's very harsh.

02:38.180 --> 02:39.840
﻿Harsh?

02:40.100 --> 02:42.390
﻿That's because, Antonio is such a terrible person!

02:43.270 --> 02:46.100
﻿Of course, he's doing some very dirty things...

02:46.270 --> 02:50.310
﻿But, Nadja, every person has their own reasons.

02:50.400 --> 02:51.270
﻿That's right.

02:51.270 --> 02:55.360
﻿There's no one who is 100% good or 100% bad.

02:56.530 --> 02:57.740
﻿Geez!

02:57.740 --> 03:00.950
﻿--You just don't know how terrible he really is!

03:01.280 --> 03:03.870
I know! Granny, I'm sure you understand, don't you?'

03:05.620 --> 03:07.830
﻿How about another cup of tea?

03:08.210 --> 03:09.580
﻿Granny... you too?

03:12.960 --> 03:14.710
﻿Antonio is terrible, isn't he?

03:20.470 --> 03:21.220
﻿Well now,

03:22.350 --> 03:23.430
﻿We're in Venice!

03:23.560 --> 03:25.220
﻿Everyone! Let's get off here!

03:25.810 --> 03:26.600
﻿Get off?!

03:32.040 --> 03:37.010
Venice, The Tearful Mama Mia

03:40.410 --> 03:42.280
﻿How beautiful!

03:44.410 --> 03:45.790
﻿It's great!

03:45.790 --> 03:48.120
﻿This is the City of Canals, Venice...!

03:53.320 --> 03:55.980
Venice, called the City of Canals,

03:55.980 --> 04:01.370
is a city made up of over 120 islands in shallow water, connected by over 40 bridges.

04:01.570 --> 04:07.580
And in Nadja's time, as it is now, automobiles could not enter the heart of the city.

04:08.140 --> 04:10.020
﻿Carrying love, hopes, and dreams...

04:10.190 --> 04:13.440
﻿We have arrived! Everyone's favorite, Dandelion Troupe!

04:13.690 --> 04:15.940
﻿As of tomorrow, here in Piazza San Marco,

04:15.940 --> 04:19.530
﻿we will put on great performances both lively and brilliant!

04:28.540 --> 04:31.500
﻿Well now, well now. Today is just a sample of that performance!

04:32.210 --> 04:35.000
﻿The, miraculous dancing princess who has set down in Venice, Nadja!

04:35.170 --> 04:40.420
﻿And, the samurai who has come here from the golden land of Jipang, Rennosuke?!

05:02.530 --> 05:04.990
﻿Venice is so nice.

05:07.700 --> 05:10.450
﻿Venetian wine is really nice.

05:11.370 --> 05:13.120
﻿Hey, Harvey?

05:13.330 --> 05:15.580
﻿It's the first holiday you've been able to get in a while...

05:15.710 --> 05:18.040
Let's go sightseeing on a gondola.

05:18.050 --> 05:19.170
﻿Wait, wait...

05:19.170 --> 05:23.130
﻿It is the first holiday I've had, that's why I want to relax.

05:24.760 --> 05:27.680
﻿WHAT?! "Black Rose appears in Milan"?!

05:27.760 --> 05:28.600
﻿Black Rose?

05:29.010 --> 05:31.600
﻿He's in Italy as well...?

05:31.850 --> 05:33.690
﻿Could this be fate?

05:33.940 --> 05:35.560
﻿It's just a coincidence.

05:35.810 --> 05:38.150
﻿Okay! I've got to talk to the editor!

05:38.150 --> 05:40.280
﻿Wha...! He's going to work after all.

05:44.570 --> 05:46.610
﻿I wanted to ride a gondola, too...

05:47.680 --> 05:51.220
La-la-lan-lan-lan, La-la-lan-lan-lan, La-la let's everybody dance!

05:50.660 --> 05:51.750
This song is...!

05:51.220 --> 05:54.850
La-la-lan-lan-lan, La-la-lan-lan-lan, La-la Let's everybody sing!

05:52.580 --> 05:57.540
﻿Everyone, we kindly hope to see you all at our performances starting tomorrow!

05:54.850 --> 05:58.400
Girls and boys, ladies and gentlemen!

05:58.400 --> 06:02.070
Welcome, welcome, to a world of dreams!

06:03.760 --> 06:04.510
﻿I knew it!

06:05.220 --> 06:06.930
﻿Nadja~!

06:05.660 --> 06:08.950
How do you do? How do you do? Nice to meet you...

06:08.390 --> 06:09.600
﻿T.J.!

06:09.160 --> 06:12.540
...the people of Canada!

06:09.970 --> 06:12.220
That we should meet in a place like this,

06:12.540 --> 06:16.250
Enchante! Enchante! Nice to meet you...

06:12.560 --> 06:14.350
﻿It must be fate!!!

06:15.060 --> 06:16.230
﻿It's just a coincidence.

06:16.330 --> 06:19.500
...people of Switzerland!

06:17.150 --> 06:19.520
﻿K-Kennosuke... what's with you?

06:19.500 --> 06:23.380
Muito prazer! Nice to meet you...

06:19.520 --> 06:20.480
﻿You're still here?

06:21.280 --> 06:22.400
﻿Of course!

06:22.400 --> 06:24.940
﻿Nadja and I are always together.

06:23.380 --> 06:26.890
...the people of Brazil!

06:27.010 --> 06:30.510
Kosh'halam az di'dane sho'ma! Nice to meet you...

06:28.280 --> 06:31.580
Why ﻿are you and Nadja wearing matching clothes?!

06:30.510 --> 06:33.560
...the people of Persia!

06:31.740 --> 06:33.580
﻿It's what's called a "pair-look'

06:35.750 --> 06:37.040
﻿Pair look...?

06:37.960 --> 06:40.250
﻿It's the costume for the Italian flag show.

06:38.020 --> 06:40.980
La-la-lan-lan-lan, La-la-lan-lan-lan, La-la Let's everybody sing!

06:40.980 --> 06:44.490
Girls and boys, monsieurs and mademoiselles!

06:42.340 --> 06:44.010
Oh....it's just a costume?

06:44.090 --> 06:45.970
﻿We dance with just the two of us, y'know.

06:44.490 --> 06:48.450
Let's hold hands all over the world, we are all friends!

06:47.220 --> 06:49.680
﻿B-B-B-But...!

06:49.680 --> 06:52.260
﻿It's more refreshing and attractive to meet once in a while, right?

06:53.020 --> 06:54.310
﻿What are you talking about?

06:54.640 --> 06:55.640
﻿Jealous?

06:55.730 --> 06:57.190
﻿Like hell!

06:59.100 --> 07:00.650
﻿I'm going to change and go for a walk.

07:02.650 --> 07:05.990
﻿Oh!! Wait, Nadja!!

07:12.790 --> 07:16.000
﻿Look! She's mad, because of you!

07:16.000 --> 07:17.370
﻿What did you say?

07:17.500 --> 07:18.960
﻿It's your fault!

07:18.960 --> 07:19.870
﻿What?!

07:20.250 --> 07:20.790
﻿You...!

07:20.790 --> 07:21.580
﻿You always...!

07:21.590 --> 07:24.000
You made the same mistake in Paris!

07:24.000 --> 07:25.170
﻿You were the one who did that!

07:25.170 --> 07:27.170
﻿I did not! You did!

07:27.170 --> 07:27.760
﻿It was you! You!

07:27.760 --> 07:28.590
What?!

07:28.680 --> 07:30.260
﻿Stop it you two!!!

07:32.850 --> 07:34.140
﻿Kennosuke!

07:34.640 --> 07:35.600
T.J.!

07:47.780 --> 07:48.860
﻿Hey!!

07:49.320 --> 07:52.070
﻿Don't you know it's dangerous to fool around while crossing a bridge?!

07:52.410 --> 07:54.370
﻿I-I'm sorry...

08:01.830 --> 08:03.000
﻿Here, eat up.

08:05.130 --> 08:09.130
﻿It's minestrone soup cooked over a slow fire, full of vitamins.

08:09.380 --> 08:11.180
﻿We have to warm up your bodies.

08:11.510 --> 08:12.300
﻿Yes, ma'am.

08:13.470 --> 08:15.390
﻿Here Nadja, you eat too.

08:15.390 --> 08:16.140
﻿Y-Yes, ma'am.

08:21.230 --> 08:22.310
﻿It's delicious!

08:22.520 --> 08:24.690
﻿Of course. This is my special soup.

08:27.820 --> 08:28.690
﻿Mrs. Irma...

08:28.990 --> 08:30.990
﻿Thank you for your help!

08:31.110 --> 08:33.280
﻿T-Thank you!!

08:33.870 --> 08:37.240
I'm glad my son's old clothes came in handy.

08:37.910 --> 08:39.410
﻿Kennosuke...

08:39.910 --> 08:42.330
﻿Your hair is still wet!

08:42.330 --> 08:44.710
﻿What are you going to do if you catch cold?

08:46.840 --> 08:48.000
﻿What are you doing?

08:48.010 --> 08:50.170
﻿You have to make sure to dry it with a towel!

08:54.300 --> 08:56.140
﻿.Just like my dead mother...

09:00.560 --> 09:05.020
﻿My mother... She also used to scold me when I got in trouble...

09:05.440 --> 09:07.980
﻿But, she was always kind and warm.

09:08.860 --> 09:10.490
﻿My mother, too...

09:16.740 --> 09:18.530
﻿Is that right?

09:18.540 --> 09:19.990
﻿So, I'm like your mothers?

09:20.290 --> 09:23.500
﻿You two are lucky to have memories of your mother.

09:24.290 --> 09:25.710
﻿Then, Nadja, you are...?

09:26.630 --> 09:29.710
﻿I was sent to an orphan when I was a baby...

09:29.920 --> 09:31.420
﻿So, I don't remember anything.

09:31.800 --> 09:36.590
﻿But recently. I found out that my mother may be alive somewhere!

09:39.640 --> 09:42.810
Um... P-P-Please don't worry!

09:42.940 --> 09:46.690
﻿The director of the orphanage treated me kindly, as a mother would...

09:48.150 --> 09:50.610
﻿You'll meet her, I know you will!

09:50.940 --> 09:53.950
﻿Your mother is probably looking for you somewhere too.

09:54.200 --> 09:56.990
She's probably thinking about you, wherever she may be.

09:59.450 --> 10:00.490
﻿Mrs. Irma...

10:01.000 --> 10:03.660
﻿So that you may meet your mother as soon as possible,

10:03.870 --> 10:06.330
﻿I'll pray for you every night.

10:17.590 --> 10:19.390
﻿Is this you in this picture?

10:21.220 --> 10:24.930
Ahh, my son drew that for me, when he was small.

10:25.480 --> 10:27.350
﻿He's the one who used to wear these clothes, right?

10:27.770 --> 10:29.400
﻿"Mama mia"?

10:30.570 --> 10:32.900
﻿It means, "my mother".

10:33.360 --> 10:34.400
﻿Mama mia...

10:35.150 --> 10:36.360
﻿My mother.

10:36.990 --> 10:40.370
﻿My husband was... a gondolier, you see.

10:41.240 --> 10:43.870
﻿But, he died of an illness when our son was still a baby.

10:44.330 --> 10:49.500
﻿After that, I became a gondolier and raised my only son.

10:52.090 --> 10:54.300
﻿He was such a kind boy.

10:56.680 --> 10:59.340
﻿I would get blisters when I was still new to this job...

10:59.470 --> 11:01.720
﻿And every night, he would put medicine on them for me.

11:02.770 --> 11:03.970
﻿Mama mia...

11:04.180 --> 11:06.600
﻿I want to grow up fast...

11:06.600 --> 11:08.230
﻿I want to grow up quickly...

11:08.230 --> 11:10.350
﻿And become a very, very rich man...

11:10.610 --> 11:14.190
﻿And, make you the happiest person in Venice.

11:22.450 --> 11:24.830
﻿That's what he promised me...

11:25.080 --> 11:27.750
﻿So what does he do now?

11:27.870 --> 11:33.540
﻿He left home and is now working very hard whilst traveling all over Europe.

11:34.340 --> 11:35.760
﻿I wish I could meet him.

11:36.720 --> 11:37.720
﻿I know!

11:38.220 --> 11:41.930
﻿We're traveling performers and we travel to many countries!

11:42.050 --> 11:45.520
﻿We might run into your son somewhere.

11:46.850 --> 11:48.480
﻿If you meet Antonio somewhere...

11:48.480 --> 11:52.020
﻿Tell him about me, get him to treat you to some gelato.

11:52.360 --> 11:53.310
﻿What?!

11:53.480 --> 11:54.480
﻿Antonio?!

11:54.820 --> 11:57.490
﻿Mrs. Irma, your son's name is Antonio?

11:59.070 --> 12:01.740
﻿He has the same name, but what a difference from that man!

12:02.490 --> 12:03.910
﻿Who is "that man"?

12:04.370 --> 12:06.450
He's an absolutely terrible man!

12:06.620 --> 12:09.910
﻿He thinks the world is all about money.

12:10.290 --> 12:13.920
﻿In order to make money, he thinks nothing of using people!

12:15.130 --> 12:16.590
﻿What a terrible man!

12:16.800 --> 12:20.590
﻿Bring him here next time, and I'll spank his bottom about a hundred times for you!

12:26.220 --> 12:27.520
﻿Please, do!

12:27.720 --> 12:29.430
﻿His name is Antonio Fabiani, and...

12:29.890 --> 12:32.350
﻿Antonio Fabiani, you say...? Then..

12:33.190 --> 12:35.400
﻿He has the same name as my son.

12:35.770 --> 12:37.190
﻿What!!!

12:58.960 --> 13:00.170
﻿I can't believe it...

13:01.090 --> 13:04.050
﻿To think that Mrs. Irma's son is that Antonio!

13:04.600 --> 13:07.930
﻿The Antonio Mrs. Irma speaks of and the one we know...

13:07.930 --> 13:09.310
﻿are like night and day, don't you think?

13:09.390 --> 13:10.100
﻿Yeah...

13:10.600 --> 13:13.020
﻿Does this mean that, he was kind when he was young,

13:13.020 --> 13:16.360
﻿but became a bad person when he grew up?

13:17.070 --> 13:18.480
I ﻿wonder...

13:21.670 --> 13:22.590
Mrs. Irma...

13:23.530 --> 13:25.820
﻿She must be so worried...

13:29.490 --> 13:31.790
﻿There's... there's no mistake...

13:35.540 --> 13:39.170
﻿That Antonio, is my son Antonio!

13:40.210 --> 13:41.590
﻿Mrs. Irma...

13:45.090 --> 13:47.970
﻿But why would that child do such a thing?

13:49.220 --> 13:54.690
﻿My mother too, was always very worried when I was bad.

13:54.940 --> 13:56.600
﻿My mother too.

13:56.810 --> 13:59.400
﻿The director at Applefield too.

14:19.210 --> 14:20.540
﻿Antonio...

14:21.300 --> 14:25.130
﻿Why-arc you acting in such a shameful way?

14:30.560 --> 14:31.760
﻿Mrs. Irma!

14:31.850 --> 14:32.850
﻿Are you there?

14:32.850 --> 14:33.980
﻿Please, let us in!

14:35.310 --> 14:37.310
﻿Uh, um, Mrs. Irma?

14:37.650 --> 14:41.980
﻿Just now, we called Antonia "terrible", But... Um...

14:41.980 --> 14:43.030
﻿Wh-What is it?

14:43.240 --> 14:45.190
How can I say this? Um...

14:45.200 --> 14:45.740
That is...

14:45.740 --> 14:46.860
﻿Please don't worry!

14:49.530 --> 14:50.570
﻿You all...!

14:53.750 --> 14:54.870
﻿Mrs. Irma...

15:04.720 --> 15:06.050
﻿Thank you...

15:07.300 --> 15:10.260
﻿You were worried about me, weren't you?

15:11.720 --> 15:14.640
﻿What kind children you all are!

15:18.310 --> 15:19.400
﻿Mama mia...

15:19.940 --> 15:21.520
﻿Mama mia...

15:34.910 --> 15:36.660
﻿To tell you the truth,

15:37.210 --> 15:41.380
﻿I did suspect that maybe he was doing something bad.

15:41.540 --> 15:43.210
﻿I just had that feeling...

15:43.360 --> 15:43.780
What...?

15:45.710 --> 15:47.670
﻿When he was sixteen years old,

15:47.800 --> 15:49.970
﻿he left for Milan to work.

16:00.020 --> 16:01.440
﻿Mama...

16:02.020 --> 16:05.820
﻿The first Dodge of Venice was a former gondolier, wasn't he?

16:06.490 --> 16:11.280
﻿If I work to the fullest of my abilities, I'm sure that someday I can become a rich man, too.

16:11.910 --> 16:14.780
﻿Then I can give you an easier life!

16:15.990 --> 16:21.920
﻿After that, he sent me a little money every month from his salary.

16:27.170 --> 16:29.470
﻿And on my birthdays and on Christmas,

16:29.670 --> 16:32.180
﻿He always sent me a very heartfelt card.

16:32.890 --> 16:34.800
But, about three years ago...

16:37.060 --> 16:40.480
﻿He told me, the business he started was doing well...

16:40.890 --> 16:43.810
﻿And sent me an unbelievable amount of money.

16:44.400 --> 16:48.320
﻿Since then, the presents he sent me for my birthdays and Christmas,

16:48.320 --> 16:51.030
﻿were things like gold necklaces and fur coats,

16:51.150 --> 16:52.990
﻿that gradually became more expensive.

16:54.200 --> 16:58.040
﻿And, his few letters were all about how much money he was making...

16:58.410 --> 17:00.330
﻿thought, "What happened to my child?"

17:00.460 --> 17:02.370
﻿It's been constantly on my mind.

17:03.130 --> 17:06.420
﻿But, I had no idea he was doing anything so bad.

17:09.670 --> 17:10.840
﻿Mrs. Irma!

17:11.340 --> 17:14.550
﻿If I see Antonio, I'm going to tell him...

17:15.180 --> 17:15.720
﻿What?

17:16.350 --> 17:18.760
﻿...that "Making your mother worry like this...

17:18.970 --> 17:20.720
﻿is completely unforgivable!"

17:21.270 --> 17:22.390
﻿That's right!

17:22.480 --> 17:23.690
﻿I'll tell him, too!

17:24.150 --> 17:25.600
﻿I'll tell him that,

17:25.610 --> 17:30.650
﻿"If you do anything bad again, you'll never be able to eat Mrs. Irma's minestrone again!"

17:30.650 --> 17:32.860
﻿Yeah! That'll teach him!

17:32.860 --> 17:34.160
﻿Right, Mrs. Irma?

17:34.740 --> 17:37.240
﻿Yeah, you're right!

17:37.910 --> 17:40.160
﻿Please, give him a good scolding for me.

17:40.750 --> 17:44.750
﻿I'm going to write him a letter tonight and give him hell!

17:45.290 --> 17:48.790
﻿I'll show you how strong an Italian Mama is!

18:01.930 --> 18:04.270
﻿I think I understand it a little now.

18:05.480 --> 18:06.810
﻿What Sylvie and the others were saying...

18:07.150 --> 18:11.150
﻿That there's no one who's 100% bad or 100% good.

18:12.110 --> 18:12.900
﻿Yeah.

18:19.330 --> 18:21.330
﻿But, I'm glad!

18:21.500 --> 18:23.160
﻿Mrs. Irma's not depressed anymore.

18:23.500 --> 18:24.120
﻿Yeah!!

18:24.290 --> 18:25.210
I'm glad, too.

18:25.210 --> 18:26.790
﻿I'm not glad at all!

18:29.130 --> 18:30.250
﻿Herbie!

18:31.050 --> 18:32.630
﻿Hey, long time no see!

18:32.960 --> 18:34.380
﻿Herbie!!

18:36.550 --> 18:37.640
﻿You!

18:37.720 --> 18:40.930
﻿You went off without a word! I've been looking all over for you!

18:43.540 --> 18:44.870
Geez!

18:46.310 --> 18:47.440
﻿By the way, Nadja.

18:47.850 --> 18:51.480
﻿Since we parted in Paris, there's something that's actually been bothering me...

18:51.860 --> 18:52.400
﻿Huh?

19:01.030 --> 19:04.120
﻿The two who were chasing you around in Paris...

19:04.370 --> 19:07.370
﻿They were after this ring and brooch, right?

19:08.460 --> 19:09.120
﻿Yes...

19:10.040 --> 19:12.840
﻿They appeared suddenly during the fire at the orphanage.

19:18.090 --> 19:21.720
﻿Hmm, I've been trying to deduce what I've heard from your story.

19:22.310 --> 19:28.190
﻿Nadja, there seems to be no doubt that your mother is from a noble house somewhere.

19:28.540 --> 19:29.250
What?

19:29.630 --> 19:30.540
Noble?

19:30.770 --> 19:31.650
﻿My mother?

19:31.900 --> 19:32.610
﻿What?

19:36.400 --> 19:37.570
﻿The problem is...

19:37.990 --> 19:42.410
﻿There is someone who thinks that your existence stands in their way.

19:42.410 --> 19:43.080
﻿In their way...?

19:43.470 --> 19:44.140
Yeah...

19:44.790 --> 19:51.580
﻿That someone wants to erase the fact that you are the child of that noble mother.

19:51.880 --> 19:53.540
﻿B-But why?

19:54.000 --> 19:55.420
﻿I don't know the reason...

19:55.710 --> 19:56.510
﻿But...

19:57.050 --> 20:01.510
﻿That brooch is an important clue that connects, you to your mother.

20:02.100 --> 20:05.310
﻿The fact that they are trying to steal it, is the most obvious proof.

20:05.310 --> 20:06.640
﻿Oh, no...!

20:07.850 --> 20:09.690
﻿What lowly scoundrels!

20:09.690 --> 20:11.440
﻿Yeah, it's not fair!

20:11.980 --> 20:13.310
﻿Listen, Nadja...

20:13.440 --> 20:17.440
﻿Never forget that they are after you. Just be careful.

20:19.720 --> 20:20.260
Yes!

20:28.040 --> 20:31.170
﻿All I want, is to meet my mother...

20:31.580 --> 20:34.420
﻿I don't care about nobility or anything else...

20:34.790 --> 20:35.880
﻿Mother...

20:36.840 --> 20:38.510
﻿I know you're alive somewhere...

20:39.380 --> 20:43.140
﻿You're probably worrying about me just like Mrs. Irma...

20:43.530 --> 20:49.080
Above a quiet forest...

20:49.080 --> 20:54.790
A single shining star,

20:54.790 --> 21:00.090
sings a song of love...

21:00.220 --> 21:05.850
The wind blows gently over the farm.

21:04.410 --> 21:05.320
﻿Mother...

21:06.180 --> 21:11.270
Little birds and kids,

21:11.270 --> 21:16.440
are held by their mothers.

21:16.610 --> 21:22.360
What plays inside a dream,

21:22.490 --> 21:29.950
is a blooming, fragrant garden

21:27.560 --> 21:28.640
﻿Nadja...

21:29.310 --> 21:31.230
﻿My darling Nadja...

21:33.230 --> 21:37.940
﻿I wonder if you can see this moon too from where you are in heaven?

21:34.080 --> 21:39.550
The day that is passing by...

21:39.550 --> 21:45.090
its smiles I hold in my hand.

21:45.220 --> 21:50.850
Good night, good night...

21:50.850 --> 21:54.310
In this hand...

21:54.310 --> 22:02.110
My dearest child...

22:15.370 --> 22:18.620
Paris is sunnier than London

22:15.370 --> 22:18.620
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

22:18.740 --> 22:21.830
Carmen likes paella more than pasta

22:18.740 --> 22:21.830
CARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

22:22.250 --> 22:28.420
The Queen of Spades is a fickle person

22:22.250 --> 22:28.420
SUPEEDO no jou kimagure yasan

22:29.380 --> 22:30.620
Indeed

22:29.380 --> 22:30.620
Kitto

22:33.380 --> 22:35.800
It's not use worrying about it

22:33.380 --> 22:35.800
Nayan datte MUDA yo

22:36.380 --> 22:39.510
Que sera sera, sera Sera

22:36.380 --> 22:39.510
KE SERA SERA SERA SERA

22:39.770 --> 22:44.480
Tomorrow's going to be whatever it was meant

22:39.770 --> 22:44.480
Ashita nante itsumo naru you ni

22:44.560 --> 22:45.940
To be, to be

22:44.560 --> 22:45.940
Naru naru

